    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and it passes. The full build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change adds an immutable structured audit event alongside the existing audit line, emitted from the create-owner pipeline's `audit` step.\n\n**New file \u2014 `OwnerCreatedEvent.java`**: an immutable value holding `seq`, `ownerId`, the primary identifier, and `membershipLevel`.\n- `seq` comes from a process-wide `AtomicLong`, so it's **monotonically increasing across all creates** (not per-request).\n- `toJson()` serializes to the exact single-line shape `{seq, ownerId, customerCode, membershipLevel, event:\"OWNER_CREATED\"}` with proper string escaping.\n- The identifier value is resolved through one private accessor, `primaryIdentifierOf(owner)`, which returns `customerCode` today. **This is the single point that changes** when the customer code is later unified into `memberId` \u2014 the callers and JSON shape stay untouched, satisfying the forward-compatibility requirement.\n\n**Edit \u2014 `AuditOwnerCreated.java`**: after the human-readable audit line, it now also emits `AUDIT.info(\"{}\", OwnerCreatedEvent.of(owner, level).toJson())`, reusing the already-computed capped `membershipLevel`. It runs after `SaveOwner` (within the transaction governance), so `owner.getId()` is populated.\n\nVerified in the logs \u2014 both events emit:\n```\nINFO AUDIT - owner created id=11 customerCode=NSW-16E6609E ... membershipLevel=1 membershipNumber=NSW-16E6609E-M27\nINFO AUDIT - {\"seq\":1,\"ownerId\":11,\"customerCode\":\"NSW-16E6609E\",\"membershipLevel\":1,\"event\":\"OWNER_CREATED\"}\n```\n\n`AcceptanceTest` (the only test class) passes and the full `mvn test` build is `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
